`Cmd/Move.pm:116-121`, `Cmd/Pick.pm:154-156`, versus
`../kanban-md/internal/task/lifecycle.go`:

    karr move 1 done; karr move 1 todo
    git show <ref>:data -> status: todo
                           completed: 2026-08-09    # stays behind

- `completed` is never cleared on reopen (Go clears it)
- `started` is set only for the literal `'in-progress'` (Go: on the first move
  out of the *first configured* status)
- `completed` is set only for the literal `'done'` (Go: any terminal status)
- a direct move to a terminal status sets `started` in Go, not in karr
- karr writes `started: 2026-08-09` (date only) while `created`/`updated`/
  `claimed_at` are full `...Z` timestamps

The last one matters beyond parity: the planned `metrics` command (lead time,
cycle time, flow efficiency) cannot compute anything meaningful from a date-only
`started`, and a stale `completed` makes every reopened task look finished.

Fix before metrics is built, or metrics will be built on wrong data.
Fixed and merged into main (3dac607); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. Note the #68 trigger change: started is now stamped on the first move out
of the FIRST CONFIGURED status, per kanban-md lifecycle.go, not out of the
literal in-progress.
